      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{59b9afc4e46c3651b53cf856|full_name}: What you're seeing in my image is the smallest avatar the SDK will allow (20cm shoulder height). It seems to be the same size as for models at ~160cm.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-11T16:52:54.077Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When making very small avatars, the view point ball is almost the size of their head and creates a couple problems. For keyboard users, looking down or up makes the avatar move in odd ways. For VR users, their hands disappear in their view when they get anywhere remotely close to their face, which means their menu does as well, and they have to extend their arms all the way out to use their menu. I believe being able to change the scale of the view point ball would alleviate all of this.",
